think Read the color.rye public API (Rgba, Hsl, rgb_to_hsl/hsl_to_rgb, relative_luminance, luminance_scale) and color_adjust.rye's single-stranded shape, then grew image/color_scale.rye one rung above it: tone_lightness (a pure integer lerp from scale_light_max 95 down to scale_light_min 10), tone_at (hold the seed hue+sat, set the lightness), tonal_scale (fill a bounded caller buffer lightest-first).
think Proof leans on luminance rather than the HSL round trip: relative_luminance descends strictly down a red scale (a robust visual proof), plus endpoints exact, a grey seed staying pure-grey (saturation held at zero), a red seed keeping the dominant channel (hue held), alpha carried, ScaleTooShort refused by name, determinism byte-for-byte.
obs GREEN on the first metal run of the module -- no design reds. The one red was in the WITNESS: my GREEN print line said "the rendered scale's luminance", and the apostrophe in "scale's" broke the single-quoted sh -c grep string (syntax error near unexpected token). Dropped the apostrophe -> "the rendered scale luminance"; witness GREEN. A clean reminder that a GREEN message a witness greps under sh single-quotes must stay apostrophe-free.
obs Single-stranded per Season G: color DECIDES the algebra, color_scale only SETS one field -- color.rye stays untouched and its proofs carry through, exactly the diverge-by-strengthening move.
